2.4 ✅ Check-in: Data Wrangling
Question 1: Suppose we would like to study how the ratio of penguin body mass to flipper size differs across the species. Arrange the following steps into an order that accomplishes this goal (assuming the steps are connected with a |&gt; or a %&gt;%).

# a
arrange(med_mass_flipper_ratio)


# b
group_by(species)


# c
penguins 


# d
summarize(
  med_mass_flipper_ratio = median(mass_flipper_ratio)
)


# e
mutate(
  mass_flipper_ratio = body_mass_g / flipper_length_mm
)







TipTry running the code!



You can check your answers using the penguins data from the palmerpenguins R package!


